{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A provenance and conservation account for the WORLD_MODEL profile. It reports how predecessor WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md rows were restated, generalized, relocated, or classified as headings without claims. Its routes are provenance only; its conservation assertions are source claims rather than independently established equivalence.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1253,
          "quote": "Rows of rc.2 WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md received by this member. Anchors are\ninto rc.2 WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md; a locus is a section of this file unless\nanother member is named. Every conserved row is restated in this\nmember's own text; a route is provenance only.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL.md#WORLD_MODEL%2F15.%20Source%20dispositions",
          "start_line":1250
        }
      ],
      "key": "world_model_disposition_account",
      "label": "WORLD_MODEL source-disposition account"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The guide owns practical writing discipline for method surfaces: core and style rules, removable habits, good and bad prose, alignment with authority layers, specification practice, layer checks, and current-surface writing. It consumes but does not define the specification chain, layers, surface rule, release boundary, or commentary layer.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":121,
          "quote": "during a change wave prefer terms such as active, current, base, live,",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F9.%20Current-surface%20writing",
          "start_line":121
        },
        {
          "end_line":11,
          "quote": "Guide. Owns the practical writing discipline for this method's surfaces:\nthe core rule, style rules, habits to remove, the marks of good and bad\nprose, alignment of tone with the authority layer, practice for\nspecification artifacts, the layer checks and present-tense writing of the\ncurrent surface. Consumes [SPEC_METHOD §2](SPEC_METHOD.md#2-the-chain)\n(the chain, its layers and the specification surface rule) and\n[§6](SPEC_METHOD.md#6-lineage-and-release) (the release version boundary),\nand [POSTING_GUIDE](POSTING_GUIDE.md) (the commentary layer); defines none\nof them.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "writing_guide",
      "label": "Writing Guide"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The referenced constitutional owner of specification-layer roles and closure, identified as SPEC_METHOD §2. The supplied writing guide supplies practice rather than redefining that owner.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":88,
          "quote": "[SPEC_METHOD §2](SPEC_METHOD.md#2-the-chain) is the constitutional\nauthority for the roles and closure of the specification layers; this\nguide supplies the practical writing discipline for those artifacts (P6;\nrc.2 #specification-artifact-practice).",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/WRITING_GUIDE.md#WRITING_GUIDE%2F7.%20Specification%20artifact%20practice",
          "start_line":85
        }
      ],
      "key": "specification_layer_authority_reference",
      "label": "Referenced specification-layer authority"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Draft 2020-12 schema urn:stdo:schema:installed-release-manifest:1 describes deterministic identity and an exact installed-member inventory for one immutable STDO RC cut. Its domains include release identity, standards and plugin member sets, individual members, LICENSE, and a release note.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":5,
          "quote": "  \"$id\": \"urn:stdo:schema:installed-release-manifest:1\",\n  \"title\": \"STDO Installed Release Manifest\",\n  \"description\": \"Deterministic identity and exact installed-member inventory for one immutable STDO RC cut.\",",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/schemas/installed-release-manifest.schema.json#preamble",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "installed_release_manifest",
      "label": "Installed Release Manifest"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Draft 2020-12 schema urn:stdo:schema:product-definition:3 describes layout-neutral bindings for one product WHAT: identity, enclosing bounded context, constitution, local constitutional relations, collective reference-frame bases, WHAT, HOW, work carriers, bootstrap, and composition.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":5,
          "quote": "  \"$id\": \"urn:stdo:schema:product-definition:3\",\n  \"title\": \"STDO Product Definition Overlay\",\n  \"description\": \"Layout-neutral exact STDO basis, identity, authority-location, bounded-context disambiguation, collective reference-frame basis, realization, work-carrier, bootstrap, and composition bindings for one STDO-defined product WHAT.\",",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json#preamble",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "product_definition_overlay",
      "label": "Product Definition Overlay"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The overlay's STDO binding separates a source Git repository, a mutable version-line discovery selector carried by an annotated Git tag, and an exact immutable installed release basis with its installed-manifest digest.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":319,
          "quote": "          \"description\": \"Mutable version-line discovery selector carried by an annotated Git tag. It is never operative constitutional authority without digest-bound explicit resolution and adoption.\"",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json#preamble",
          "start_line":319
        },
        {
          "end_line":334,
          "quote": "              \"description\": \"Digest of the deterministic installed-release manifest carrying tag, commit, tree, and complete distribution identity.\"",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json#preamble",
          "start_line":334
        }
      ],
      "key": "product_stdo_binding",
      "label": "Product STDO binding"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A scoped local term-resolution record identifies a resolution carrier, exact lexical term, bounded-context identity, complete material candidate references, selected concept, existing lawful authorities, semantic bases, and governed scopes. A label alone is not a context-free concept identity.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":470,
          "quote": "          \"description\": \"Exact lexical label being resolved; the label is not a context-free concept identity.\"",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json#preamble",
          "start_line":470
        },
        {
          "end_line":478,
          "quote": "          \"description\": \"Complete material candidate concept or clause references for the declared term, context, basis, and scope.\"",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json#preamble",
          "start_line":478
        }
      ],
      "key": "local_term_disambiguation",
      "label": "Local term disambiguation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The AGENTS template contains a marker-bounded STDO bootstrap block, starting with STDO_BOOTSTRAP_START and ending with STDO_BOOTSTRAP_END. It represents routing and prerequisite instructions for constitutional work; it is not an operative activation in this interpretation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1,
          "quote": "<!-- STDO_BOOTSTRAP_START -->",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/AGENTS_TEMPLATE.md#preamble",
          "start_line":1
        },
        {
          "end_line":20,
          "quote": "<!-- STDO_BOOTSTRAP_END -->",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/AGENTS_TEMPLATE.md#STDO%20Bootstrap",
          "start_line":20
        }
      ],
      "key": "agents_bootstrap_template",
      "label": "AGENTS bootstrap template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The CLAUDE template separately contains a marker-bounded STDO bootstrap block. Its matching text does not merge its document identity with the AGENTS template or instantiate an activation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1,
          "quote": "<!-- STDO_BOOTSTRAP_START -->",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/CLAUDE_TEMPLATE.md#preamble",
          "start_line":1
        },
        {
          "end_line":20,
          "quote": "<!-- STDO_BOOTSTRAP_END -->",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/CLAUDE_TEMPLATE.md#STDO%20Bootstrap",
          "start_line":20
        }
      ],
      "key": "claude_bootstrap_template",
      "label": "CLAUDE bootstrap template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Project Goals is a template for current overriding project concerns, their role relative to intent, product definition and requirements, and active goals for the current work wave.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":3,
          "quote": "State the current overriding concerns for this project in present tense.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/GOALS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Goals",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "project_goals_template",
      "label": "Project Goals template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Project Intent is a template for present-tense project direction, reason for existence, required outcomes, and shaping constraints.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":3,
          "quote": "State the direction for this project in present tense.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/INTENT_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Intent",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "project_intent_template",
      "label": "Project Intent template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An illustrative JSON overlay with replace-me identities and release placeholders. It supplies a source repository example; four basis-qualified entrypoints for bootstrap, SPEC_METHOD, REFERENCE_FRAME and EXECUTIVE_BASELINE; AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md bootstrap targets; empty additional authorities, axioms, overrides, common HOW and composition; one illustrative term disambiguation; one frame-basis reference; specification, default tenant and work-carrier paths. These values demonstrate bindings rather than an accepted Product.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":10,
          "quote": "  \"$schema\": \"stdo://releases/REPLACE_WITH_IMMUTABLE_CUT/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json\",\n  \"kind\": \"stdo.product-definition\",\n  \"product\": {\n    \"definition_id\": \"urn:stdo:product-definition:replace-me\",\n    \"name\": \"Replace Me\",\n    \"source_project\": \"./\",\n    \"bounded_context\": {\n      \"id\": \"urn:stdo:bounded-context:replace-me\",\n      \"definition\": \"./specification/PRODUCT.md#product-terms\"",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/PRODUCT_DEFINITION_TEMPLATE.json#preamble",
          "start_line":2
        }
      ],
      "key": "product_definition_template",
      "label": "Product Definition JSON template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Project Product is a prose template separating current product realization, product kind and domain, context-bound Product terms, a goal model, intended end state, and a current definition decomposable into requirements.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":3,
          "quote": "State the current product realization for this project in present tense.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/PRODUCT_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Product",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "project_product_template",
      "label": "Project Product template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A structured-prose starter projecting PRODUCT_DEFINITION section 7's collective reference-frame binding. It is not authority. A completed declaration requires replacement of every placeholder and admission by existing Product, requirement, Goals, accepted-design, identity, work or release authorities owning its decisions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":7,
          "quote": "This starter projects\n`PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#7-collective-reference-frame-basis`. It is not\nauthority. Replace every placeholder and admit the completed declaration\nthrough the existing Product, requirement, Goals, accepted-design, identity,\nwork, or release authorities that own its decisions.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "project_frame_basis_template",
      "label": "Project Reference-Frame Basis template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A planning inventory for every known material evaluation. Its disposition domain is activate, non_material or residual, distinct from coverage status; applicability premises are true, false or unknown; required-result evidence is satisfied, missing or invalid.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":57,
          "quote": "- disposition: `activate | non_material | residual` (a planning choice, not\n  a coverage status; see Coverage And Residuals)\n- non-material evidence or residual and re-entry condition:\n- owning applicability predicate and true/false/unknown premises:\n- required-result identity and current satisfied/missing/invalid evidence:",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FEvaluation%20Inventory",
          "start_line":53
        }
      ],
      "key": "project_evaluation_inventory",
      "label": "Project evaluation inventory"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A project frame declaration identifies a frame independently of its actor and describes the evaluation family, manifold, coordinates, equality, invariants, authorities, evidence, actor envelope, dependencies, result routes, invalidation and qualification.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":79,
          "quote": "Actor identity and frame identity remain separate. One actor may occupy several\nframes only where every authority and independence condition remains valid.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FFrame%20Declarations%20And%20Actor%20Binding",
          "start_line":78
        }
      ],
      "key": "project_frame_declaration",
      "label": "Project frame declaration"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "The Product adopts the executive profile."
      ],
      "definition": "The optional EXECUTIVE_BASELINE coordination configuration selects dependency-ready evaluations, consumes closed results and chooses already-authorized next actions. The Executive label itself supplies no Product-meaning, implementation, mutation, acceptance or publication authority.",
      "exceptions": [
        "Another adopted configuration supplies its own coordination."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":113,
          "quote": "This section, and the Executive steps of the topology below, bind the\nexecutive configuration of `EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md`. They apply only when the\nProduct adopts that profile. Under another configuration, replace them with the\ncoordination the applicable configuration selects:",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FExecutive%20Attention%2C%20Evaluation%2C%20And%20Action",
          "start_line":110
        }
      ],
      "key": "executive_configuration",
      "label": "Executive configuration"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Claim-relative coverage and closure recording distinguishes uncovered, conditional, conflicted, unknown, excluded and out-of-frame residuals. A planning residual maps to excluded_by_authority only with explicit claim-consistent governing retention; otherwise it is conditionally_covered or uncovered. A non_material inventory row has no coverage status.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":178,
          "quote": "A `residual` row is\n`excluded_by_authority` where governing authority explicitly retains its\nresidual consistently with the claim, and otherwise `conditionally_covered` or\n`uncovered`. A `non_material` row is no material evaluation and takes no\ncoverage status; its non-material evidence stays in the inventory above.\nAvailable frame count and coordinator visibility are not coverage.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/PROJECT_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS_TEMPLATE.md#Project%20Reference-Frame%20Basis%2FCoverage%20And%20Residuals",
          "start_line":173
        }
      ],
      "key": "project_coverage_ledger",
      "label": "Project coverage and closure ledger"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Starter templates are source material for project-local specification and bootstrap files, including stdo_default.json or stdo_<label>.json, GOALS.md, INTENT.md, PRODUCT.md, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and a Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":6,
          "quote": "This directory holds starter templates for shared specification surfaces and\nagent bootstrap surfaces.\n\nUse these templates as source material for project-local files such as:",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/README.md#Standards%20Templates",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "standards_templates",
      "label": "Standards templates"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An optional human-readable companion to canonical how.build_tenants bindings. The Product Definition Overlay owns tenant identity and location. One singleton constitutional WHAT may have many independent build-tenant realizations.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":8,
          "quote": "This is an optional human-readable companion to the canonical\n`how.build_tenants` bindings in the Product's `stdo_<label>.json` definition.\n\nThe Product Definition Overlay owns build-tenant identity and location. Keep\nthis table consistent with that JSON or generate it from the definition. This\nfile must not become a second tenant registry.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/TENANT_REGISTRY_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Registry",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "tenant_registry_companion",
      "label": "Tenant Registry companion"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The common root holds project-local realization surfaces shared across more than one tenant; its design surface holds genuinely cross-tenant design law.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":3,
          "quote": "This root holds project-local realization surfaces shared across more than one tenant.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Build-Tenant%20Surfaces",
          "start_line":3
        },
        {
          "end_line":5,
          "quote": "Use this surface only for design law that genuinely applies across multiple build tenants.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Tenant%20Design",
          "start_line":5
        }
      ],
      "key": "common_realization_surfaces",
      "label": "Common realization surfaces"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Common ADRs are durable design memory for decisions governing two or more build tenants, located under common design/adrs. They are Design under SPEC_METHOD section 10, not an additional constitutional layer or a second requirement surface.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":5,
          "quote": "This folder holds the Architecture Decision Records that govern realization across two or more build tenants.\n\nADRs at this surface are the durable design memory for cross-tenant realization choices. They are the form of `Design` defined in `SPEC_METHOD.md` section 10, Design records, not a separate constitutional layer above design, and not a second requirement surface.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/README_TEMPLATE.md#Common%20Tenant%20ADRs",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "common_adr_collection",
      "label": "Common ADR collection"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A common ADR body template with local ID and short title, illustrative active status, Implements requirement references, Derives from intent or strategy/design references, Supersedes prior ADR/doctrine or none, conditional Superseded by, and Retained special case or none.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":10,
          "quote": "| `Status:` | `active` |\n| `Implements:` | `REQ-*` IDs this ADR makes true |\n| `Derives from:` | `INT-*` or strategy/design doc that motivated the decision |\n| `Supersedes:` | Prior ADR or doctrine this replaces, or `none` |\n| `Superseded by:` | Successor ADR if this one becomes `superseded`, otherwise omit |\n| `Retained special case:` | When earlier behavior is intentionally retained, or `none` |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/common/design/adrs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md#ADR-%3Clocal-id%3E%20%3CShort%20Decision%20Title%3E",
          "start_line":5
        }
      ],
      "key": "common_adr_template",
      "label": "Common ADR template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "One concrete tenant's root contains tenant-local realization, and its design directory contains tenant-local design surfaces. Its adopted common surfaces are declared explicitly; shared law remains at common/design.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":3,
          "quote": "This root holds one concrete build tenant for the project.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Root",
          "start_line":3
        },
        {
          "end_line":7,
          "quote": "Tenant-local design surfaces live here.\n\nResolve the governing method from the exact installed STDO basis in the\napplicable Product Definition and use `build_tenants/common/design/` for shared\nrealization law.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/templates/build_tenants/variant/design/README_TEMPLATE.md#Tenant%20Design",
          "start_line":3
        }
      ],
      "key": "tenant_realization_surfaces",
      "label": "Tenant realization surfaces"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Tenant ADRs govern this single build tenant and preserve durable design memory for its realization choices. They are Design under SPEC_METHOD section 10, not a constitutional layer above Design or a second requirement surface.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
